---
const repo = 'https://github.com/0xHelico/helico'
const faqs = [
	{
		q: 'What is Helico, in plain words?',
		a: 'When you put money into a trading pool, it only earns while the price stays inside a range you chose. Prices drift, and then the money sits idle. Helico watches for that and moves your deposit back into range, under rules you write down once: which pool, how wide, how often, how much must be kept. A contract checks every rule before anything moves, and blocks anything else.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Who holds my money?',
		a: 'You do. Your deposit stays in your wallet as a token that proves you own it. You give the contract permission to move it, not to keep it. A move takes your deposit out, exchanges what is needed, and puts a new deposit straight back in your name. The contract holds the funds for one step and proves, before that step ends, that it kept none.',
	},
	{
		q: 'What can the automation do to it?',
		a: 'One thing: propose a move inside your rules. It cannot pay itself, it cannot spend more than your deposit released, and it cannot send anything anywhere but back to you or into the pool. A misbehaving automation could move you within your own rules, and nothing else.',
	},
	{
		q: 'When does it do nothing?',
		a: 'Most of the time. It waits while your cooldown runs, and whenever a move would not bring the deposit meaningfully closer to the price, because every move costs a little. And the contract refuses any instruction that does not match the rules it holds for you.',
	},
	{
		q: 'What stays private?',
		a: 'How the decision is made. The program that decides runs inside a sealed environment: which deposits it watches, when it looks, and how it sizes a move never leave it. The rules themselves are public on the chain, so anyone can check that a move followed them.',
	},
	{
		q: 'Is it live? Is it audited?',
		a: 'Neither, yet. It is built for Arbitrum One. The contract has a rehearsed deployment, and the whole flow has been run end to end on a snapshot of the real market: an automated decision moved a real deposit and kept 94% of it working, and a second run correctly did nothing. That was a snapshot, not the live network, and the sealed environment was simulated. Twelve AI reviewers and then six more went over the contract; that is not a professional audit, and this page does not call it one.',
	},
]
---

<section class="wrap faq" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
	<h2 id="faq-title">FAQs</h2>
	<div class="faq__list">
		{faqs.map((f) => (
			<details class="faq__item">
				<summary>
					<span>{f.q}</span>
					<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 5v14" /><path d="M5 12h14" /></svg>
				</summary>
				<p>{f.a}</p>
			</details>
		))}
	</div>
	<p class="faq__more"><a href={`${repo}#readme`}>Learn More About Helico</a></p>
</section>

<style>
	.faq {
		max-width: 662px;
		margin-top: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6rem);
		margin-bottom: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
	}
	.faq h2 {
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
		font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3vw, 2.5rem);
		font-weight: 500;
		line-height: 1.35;
		letter-spacing: -0.02em;
		color: var(--ink-90);
	}
	.faq__item {
		border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(37, 34, 40, 0.08);
	}
	.faq__item summary {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: 1.4rem 0;
		cursor: pointer;
		list-style: none;
		font-size: 1rem;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		color: var(--ink-90);
	}
	.faq__item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}
	.faq__item summary svg {
		flex: none;
		width: 1rem;
		height: 1rem;
		color: var(--ink-65);
		transition: transform 0.2s;
	}
	.faq__item[open] summary svg {
		transform: rotate(45deg);
	}
	.faq__item p {
		margin: 0 0 1.4rem;
		font-size: 1rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		color: var(--ink-65);
	}
	.faq__more {
		margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
		font-size: 0.875rem;
		font-weight: 450;
	}
	.faq__more a {
		color: var(--lav-text);
	}
</style>
